{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRKAoL4Ne3L45uXdc2F2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mc7ZXvfvWFYFynCUcEQXC1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-rotjp0/memory/wholesale-tax-exempt.md","content":"---\nname: wholesale-tax-exempt\ndescription: Accountant rule - customers with tier \"wholesale\" are never charged tax, even in regions that have a tax rate\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nCustomers whose tier is \"wholesale\" are never charged tax, even when their region has a tax rate. The invoice tax calculation must treat them as exempt (zero tax) and never apply the regional rate.\n\n**Why:** Wholesale customers are resellers with a resale certificate. This is a rule from the company's accountant.\n\n**How to apply:** When writing or changing invoice/tax code, check the customer tier first. If it is \"wholesale\", skip the regional tax rate entirely. Add a test covering a wholesale customer in a taxed region. No code change was requested when this was recorded (2026-11-26).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":21993,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":386,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca7031d5-8847-4fa1-9c28-8672feb8d481","uuid":"fdaed421-db1a-4848-92d7-a73bfbec3ce5","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:36:54.781Z","request_id":"req_011ChRKAoD81LzvPKH8M3FPF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Mc7ZXvfvWFYFynCUcEQXC1":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-rotjp0/memory/wholesale-tax-exempt.md","content":"---\nname: wholesale-tax-exempt\ndescription: Accountant rule - customers with tier \"wholesale\" are never charged tax, even in regions that have a tax rate\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nCustomers whose tier is \"wholesale\" are never charged tax, even when their region has a tax rate. The invoice tax calculation must treat them as exempt (zero tax) and never apply the regional rate.\n\n**Why:** Wholesale customers are resellers with a resale certificate. This is a rule from the company's accountant.\n\n**How to apply:** When writing or changing invoice/tax code, check the customer tier first. If it is \"wholesale\", skip the regional tax rate entirely. Add a test covering a wholesale customer in a taxed region. No code change was requested when this was recorded (2026-11-26).\n"}}}
